# Abstract classes

## A class you can't instantiate

```java
public abstract class Shape {
    public abstract double area();     // no body — subclasses supply it
    public String describe() {         // concrete — shared
        return "A shape with area " + area();
    }
}
new Shape();   // compile error
```

Exists only to be **extended**. Fill in every abstract method → the subclass becomes concrete.

## Template methods

The base lays out the skeleton; subclasses fill the holes:

```java
public final void print() {
    header(); body(); footer();   // body() abstract; header/footer shared
}
```

## vs interface

- **Abstract class** — shared **state + implementation**, an "is-a" hierarchy; extend **one**
- **Interface** — a **capability** unrelated types implement; mix in **several**
